A. belt-belt, B18b geometry (8.4e6 rocks, 2.2-3.2 AU, 2D annulus, q_rel=1e-6):
   mean spacing 2.13e+08 m
   1-km rocks  b_cross=    16.0 m vs contact radius   2000 m -> contact per body every     71.6 yr game time (belt turnover: every body individual after ~that long)
   100-m rocks b_cross=     0.0 m vs contact radius    200 m -> contact per body every      716 yr game time (belt turnover: every body individual after ~that long)
   1-m rocks   b_cross=     0.0 m vs contact radius      2 m -> contact per body every 7.16e+04 yr game time (belt turnover: every body individual after ~that long)
   gravity between rocks: b_cross < contact radius at every rock size ->
   all mutual gravitational kicks are sub-quantum (sum exactly, 0 bits until they cross)

A2. embedded masses (planets, protoplanets, heavy fleets) - the movers:
   turnover of the whole belt in 100 kyr of game time needs M >= 8.17e+18 kg (8.17e+15 t)
   turnover of the whole belt in 1 Myr   of game time needs M >= 8.17e+17 kg (8.17e+14 t)
   turnover of the whole belt in 1 Gyr   of game time needs M >= 8.17e+14 kg (8.17e+11 t)
   one Ceres (9.4e20 kg) embedded: 26 promotions per game-day, belt fully individual after ~869 yr
   one 1e15 kg fleet (10^9 t): 1.0e-02 promotions/yr: dead term alone, alive only as aggregates (principle 6)

C. resonance chaos (mu=9.5e-04, W=0.024 a, spacing~0.027 a, coverage 91% of axis):
   f_chaos=0.05  tau_L=1e+02 orb -> crossing at  6.1e+03 yr game time, promotion rate 2.2e-06/s, H_live growth 4.1e-05 B/s
   f_chaos=0.05  tau_L=1e+04 orb -> crossing at  6.1e+05 yr game time, promotion rate 2.2e-08/s, H_live growth 4.1e-07 B/s
   f_chaos=0.30  tau_L=1e+02 orb -> crossing at  6.1e+03 yr game time, promotion rate 1.3e-05/s, H_live growth 2.5e-04 B/s
   f_chaos=0.30  tau_L=1e+04 orb -> crossing at  6.1e+05 yr game time, promotion rate 1.3e-07/s, H_live growth 2.5e-06 B/s
   (inside a strong zone the first resonant kick per conjunction is already
    above the quantum: crossing in ~orbits, not tau_L*ln(1/q); bound unchanged)
   -> monotone, bounded by f_chaos*N_belt once each; 43.9 MB per belt at f=0.3 (a 1e9-body universe of such belts: 5.2 GiB)

